 "narrative": "**SCALECRAFT SOCIAL SNAPSHOT — @talon__wilson**\n\n**WHERE YOU STAND**  \nYour overall score is 75, which shows solid performance but leaves room to grow. The biggest gaps come from Posting Consistency and Profile Clarity. Your reels are a clear strength, delivering an average engagement rate of 29.9%—far above typical travel accounts.\n\n**THE SINGLE BIGGEST OPPORTUNITY**  \nAdd a clear, clickable link and a call‑to‑action (CTA) in your bio to turn the highly‑engaged audience into website traffic, newsletter sign‑ups, or bookings. With 1,680 followers and a 29.9% engagement rate, even a modest conversion lift could generate a noticeable boost in enquiries and sales.\n\n**YOUR 30-60-90 DAY PATH**  \n1. **Days 1–30 – Boost Profile Clarity:** Update your bio today to include a clickable link to your booking page (e.g., `www.talonwilson.com/book`) and a CTA such as “Book your next adventure now.” This gives the 29.9%‑engaged audience a direct path to act.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 1–4 posting calendar  \n\n2. **Days 31–60 – Increase Posting Rhythm:** Pick three fixed posting days — Mon, Wed, Sat — and publish a reel on each. Reels already outperform other formats (average ≈ 656 engagements), so a regular reel cadence will close the current 2.1‑posts‑per‑week gap.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + content prompts  \n\n3. **Days 61–90 – Leverage Top Reel Formula:** Spend 30 minutes this week reviewing your top three reels (Sept 17 2026, Sept 12 2026, and the best carousel) and write a brief that captures the common hook (the opening line) and visual theme; schedule one new reel using that hook for the next Thursday. Replicating the proven formula should lift the low‑performing reels and keep engagement high.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + week‑by‑week posting calendar  \n\n**WHAT YOUR BEST POSTS HAVE IN COMMON**  \nYour top post on 2026‑09‑17 was a reel that earned 8,324 likes and 311 comments. The three best posts all use the reel format, feature striking landscape subjects, and were published on Thursdays with captions that start with a short, curiosity‑driving sentence. The three lowest‑performing posts are also reels but posted on Wednesdays and receive far fewer engagements (under 0.2× average), indicating timing and hook matter.\n\n**WHAT THE FULL PLAN ADDS**  \nThe remaining moves for all three phases, the detailed week‑by‑week posting calendar, and custom content prompts drawn from your own top‑performing posts.",
